    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier efficiency score of 81.88. His massive projection benefits from a 16% park factor boost and a significant platoon edge against Sean Burke. Joining him in the \"Strong\" category is **Jacob Wilson** (71.63), who leverages a favorable 4.69 xERA matchup against Eric Lauer to vault well above his base projection. We are also leaning into speed-dependent upside today; both **Heliot Ramos** and **Miguel Vargas** earn elevated scores due to matchups against Shane Baz, whose slow delivery provides the optimal environment for our base-stealing targets to exploit the battery.\n\nStrategic lineup construction forced a difficult decision regarding **Josh Lowe**, who was the closest exclusion from our starting nine with a score of 49.82. While his platoon advantage against George Kirby is attractive, the combination of a low batting order position and negative park factors ultimately pushed him behind the marginal threshold in favor of the higher-scoring **Jackson Merrill** and **Kyle Tucker**. Meanwhile, we are maintaining a watchful eye on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, both of whom carry risk due to challenging left-handed pitching assignments. Given the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, any late-breaking shifts in batting order or confirmed weather volatility could necessitate a rapid re-evaluation of the bench depth, particularly if **Nasim Nunez** or **Josh Jung** see movement in their respective roles.",
